				\begin{document}$$\Delta G=\Delta E+\Delta {{{\rm{ZPE}}}}-T\Delta S$$\end{document} Δ G = Δ E + Δ ZPE − T Δ S where Δ G  is the change in Gibbs free energy, Δ E  represents the total energy change derived from DFT calculations, ΔZPE is the change in zero-point energy, Δ S  denotes the entropy change, and  T  is the temperature (298.15 K).

